From: E App (round 7, main 2026-11-08, App 3b)
Subject: carry Brain's `ofCard` from the whiteboard intent to the client's script

Brain ships `ofCard: boolean` (shared/contracts.ts BoardSegment; tests/r7-brain-v62.test.mjs T46): on the whiteboard intent
for page 0, and on each intent.segments[] entry for its page. true = the page is the open card's own board, false = any
other board, absent = no card open (today's behaviour). The client only sees the composed script, so the question card can
fold to "Your question is waiting" (App, src/child/lesson/cardTiming.ts) only if the flag rides on it:
- shared/whiteboard.js normalizeScript keeps a boolean `ofCard` on the script and on each `switches[]` entry (it whitelists
  fields, so today both are stripped);
- board-first.js segmentsOf carries each page's flag; pagesBoard writes page 0's on the script and each later page's on
  its switch;
- seam.js drawn(): page 0's flag from the intent goes on the script for single-page boards too.
Absent stays absent everywhere (no behaviour change until Brain sends the field). Apply with `git apply`.
App's test tests/r7-app-ofcard-wire.test.mjs runs the whole chain (Brain's intent shape → segmentsOf → normalizeScript →
the App reader) once this is applied, and checks that it applies until then.

